  },
  "chapter": 493,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 19 Chapter 493\n\n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7301, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to requiring\n        certain persons providing substance  abuse  treatment  on  coun-\n        seling to complete training in medication assisted treatment\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  This  bill  would require certain substance abuse treatment counselors\nto take continuing education on Medication Assisted Treatment (MAT).\n\n  The opioid epidemic presents an ongoing crisis in New York State which\nis taking the lives of persons young and old, urban and rural, rich  and\npoor. We must continue to take an affirmative stand to help families and\ncommunities suffering from this debilitating epidemic.\n\n  MAT  is  hailed  by  experts  as  an  effective and low cost method of\ncombatting opioid addiction. However, many counselors indicate  they  do\nnot  have sufficient training and information to effectively deploy this\ntreatment method. This bill would mandate continuing education  in  MAT,\nand provide another resource for individuals in need.\n\n  The  Executive  has secured a three-way agreement with the Legislature\nto pass legislation in the upcoming session to  make  certain  technical\namendments  necessary to effectuate the important goals of this bill. On\nthat basis, I am signing this bill.\n\n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2016
 },
